### ==============================================================================
### Use this file with the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
### Server URL: http://localhost:5000
### ==============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@contentType = application/json

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### PRE-SET AUTH TOKENS (Or login below to refresh)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@adminToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpZCI6IjZhZDNkNTA2MzIzNjZkMGE3NTRlM2UzMSIsImVtYWlsIjoiYWRtaW5AZHJpdmV2dWUuY29tIiwicm9sZSI6IkFETUlOIiwiaWF0IjoxNzkyMjY4MTE2LCJleHAiOjE3OTI4NzI5MTZ9.ZqLYgpO09bNQb3Gi1AFJ24C7_lGYtTkb6Q2Sl_4FpaQ

### ==============================================================================
### STEP 1: Authentication Helpers
### ==============================================================================

### 1.1 Login as ADMIN
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@drivevue.com",
  "password": "adminpassword123"
}

###

### 1.2 Login as standard USER
# @name userLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "rahim@example.com",
  "password": "123456password"
}

### Extracted User Token
@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body.token}}

### ==============================================================================
### STEP 2: Fetch an Available Car ID for Testing
### ==============================================================================

### 2.1 Get Cars to obtain a valid car ID
# @name getCars
GET {{baseUrl}}/cars?isAvailable=true

### Set carId from first available car (or paste one manually)
@carId = {{getCars.response.body.data[0]._id}}

### ==============================================================================
### STEP 3: Booking Flow (USER Endpoints)
### ==============================================================================

### 3.1 Create a Booking (Logged-in User)
# @name createBooking
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "car": "{{carId}}",
  "startDate": "2026-11-01",
  "endDate": "2026-11-05"
}

### Save created booking ID
@bookingId = {{createBooking.response.body.data._id}}

###

### 3.2 Get My Bookings (Logged-in User)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/my-bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### 3.3 Cancel a Booking (User can cancel their own booking)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/bookings/cancel/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### ==============================================================================
### STEP 4: Admin Booking Operations
### ==============================================================================

### 4.1 Get All Bookings in the System (Admin Only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ==============================================================================
### STEP 5: Validation & Security Tests
### ==============================================================================

### 5.1 Test Create Booking Without Auth Token -> Expected: 401 Unauthorized
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "car": "{{carId}}",
  "startDate": "2026-11-01",
  "endDate": "2026-11-05"
}

###

### 5.2 Test Create Booking with Invalid Dates (End before Start) -> Expected: 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "car": "{{carId}}",
  "startDate": "2026-11-10",
  "endDate": "2026-11-05"
}

###

### 5.3 Test Non-Admin Accessing GET All Bookings -> Expected: 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### 5.4 Test Cancel Already Cancelled Booking -> Expected: 400 Bad Request
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/bookings/cancel/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
